[{:db/id "q-134529/selection/fbcf0b956e4350aa4d9f24259dc0684ef625f374c643297997b59102ef07817b" :answer/id #uuid "50506732-0e79-5a81-ae44-6d25598a764a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.52%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134529/selection/eba56308e162ef220bc90532b1f8f4909e0171997d1e1546787a96a20c6c10c9" :answer/id #uuid "d0756de8-e391-5c40-9840-3edde5e9fe77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.55%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134529/selection/562955e539283cad678af061670d2326ba4e7271c398304b67e4b69997196428" :answer/id #uuid "162ec16a-3b4d-5f4f-94ac-071a40d5c5ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.49%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134529/selection/8f1a289f056d2f67055f61adc7f1315fa208eefcc8b2f16cbdade7074602fad0" :answer/id #uuid "976b4899-7903-5cb9-82f0-93e82a108a87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.47%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134529/selection/407ebb82146c5c781bee70e4f2f7ae8c1152718a19f36696a7ccfd9fc98777c0" :answer/id #uuid "6ef46c96-0ad0-53e2-a066-4466cb3e4014" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.45%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134529/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b758f262-7cd7-5727-a4fe-c622b22ab767" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134529/selection/562955e539283cad678af061670d2326ba4e7271c398304b67e4b69997196428" :answer-field/choices ["q-134529/selection/fbcf0b956e4350aa4d9f24259dc0684ef625f374c643297997b59102ef07817b" "q-134529/selection/eba56308e162ef220bc90532b1f8f4909e0171997d1e1546787a96a20c6c10c9" "q-134529/selection/562955e539283cad678af061670d2326ba4e7271c398304b67e4b69997196428" "q-134529/selection/8f1a289f056d2f67055f61adc7f1315fa208eefcc8b2f16cbdade7074602fad0" "q-134529/selection/407ebb82146c5c781bee70e4f2f7ae8c1152718a19f36696a7ccfd9fc98777c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134529" :question/id #uuid "61a16f5c-99a6-5b86-b6ca-12e8e6087eb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-134529" :question/problem "Calculate the percentage error obtained when approximating the value of $(0.9)^{6}$ using the first three terms of the binomial expansion of $(1+x)^{6}$ in ascending powers of $x.$ Round your final percentage error to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when $n$ is a positive integer, \n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{1}{2!}n(n-1){x}^{2}+⋯+{x}^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1+x)}^{6} & =1+6x+\\frac{1}{2!}\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot {x}^{2}+⋯+{x}^{n} \\\\  & =1+6x+15{x}^{2}+⋯+{x}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for small $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(1+x)}^{6}≈1+6x+15{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=-0.1$ into the above approximation of $(1+x)^{6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0.9)^{6} & =(1+(-0.1))^{6} \\\\  & ≈1+6(-0.1)+15(-0.1)^{2} \\\\  & =1-6(0.1)+15(0.01) \\\\  & =1-0.6+0.15 \\\\  & =0.55\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using a calculator, we can compute the percentage error, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}%\\,error & =\\frac{\\text{amount of error}}{\\text{exact value}}\\times 100 \\\\  & =\\frac{|(0.9)^{6}-0.55|}{(0.9)^{6}}\\times 100 \\\\  & ≈3.49%\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-134529/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e74e4a-8641-54c9-9d9d-c3ca53c94f8f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134529"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134648/selection/b3b7ee12029a4bcabc2634f16401fe6a99c5501ac09d9e57343719371e92d375" :answer/id #uuid "04a5e696-215d-52ed-bd0a-c5653ca73a9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "227.234" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134648/selection/62c3d8e1b368ac27b4bfb3c793868d24151e6624bd6e8797f27e1b63c86b4a55" :answer/id #uuid "dc07881a-84c7-5e22-bae8-c95a028a9683" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "227.230" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134648/selecti